\title{zuroar: Compressed Sets of Unsigned Integers with 'Roaring' Bitmaps}
\description{
Compressed sets of unsigned integers from 0 to 2^32 - 1, and up to 2^64 - 1, built on a bundled copy of 'CRoaring', the reference C implementation of 'Roaring' bitmaps (Lemire et al. 2018 \doi{10.1002/spe.2560}). A bitmap answers membership, cardinality, rank, select and the set operations without materialising a vector, and serialises to the portable 'Roaring' format shared by implementations in 'Java', 'Go', 'Rust' and 'Python'. To R code a bitmap behaves as a sorted vector without duplicates.
}
